#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167890} :activity/id #uuid "18df0fdd-60be-5a81-a0cd-e95103dfb1c0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049896 :topic/id #uuid "1c8e94f0-f686-5ab0-b88e-99e6f26eaf54" :topic/math-academy-id 3232} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167886 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167982 :tutorial/content "![](images/44/44a90d0fa61d3643848f01479706cca752a00914b99185da5b8739c5e1cab182.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. In the initial value problem above, we apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation.\n\nFirst, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{5{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=5L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+6L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=5{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+6{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\n**Step 2**. Now, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns X_1(s) +  3 = 5 X_1(s)\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_1(s) = -\\dfrac{3}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns X_2(s) -  2 = -2\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{s-5}\\right) + 6 X_2(s) \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**. To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{3}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{8}{s-6}-\\frac{6}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\}-6{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ 8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a475ed27-9529-52d2-85cb-9e8827c5b45e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14201 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example"} :step/id #uuid "648d1a99-8c25-5200-8b95-382792dca052" :step/math-academy-id 590676 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167887}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167887 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166930 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166510 :question/id #uuid "0b2a74d8-1ce2-5055-a843-1456b1878cf7" :question/math-academy-id "e-21157"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd7b8fc8-26d3-5551-9a46-45725bd863a6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048605} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050098}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167162} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167206} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304952} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304953} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304954} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390939} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390955} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433217} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433219}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"} :step/id #uuid "887d1a2a-3793-57e6-a390-bcc123897754" :step/math-academy-id 590677 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167888}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167888 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166508 :question/id #uuid "d9715a0c-6808-5db8-b0b4-5bedc4f2e9e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-21155"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167159} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167163} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304955} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304957} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304958} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304963} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433218}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"} :step/id #uuid "c39529f2-6303-5dd8-a113-cdaf40a5d673" :step/math-academy-id 590680 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167889}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167889 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166509 :question/id #uuid "ec8e6fde-504e-581f-b465-6a9bc3927d77" :question/math-academy-id "e-21156"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050768}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167160} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167161} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305033} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305034} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305035} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305036} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305037}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"} :step/id #uuid "aa736c0f-1eaa-5601-a02e-62159a1f73b2" :step/math-academy-id 590683} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167890 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168031 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we'll learn how to use Laplace transforms to solve homogeneous systems like the one below.\n![](images/66/66eb9ce1b87b67ba550fc0b76493b775bf2b2e67be257b9fe9974db9d53cdffa.svg)\n\nThe process can be split into three steps.\n\n- **Step 1.** Apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation, to get a system with variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Solve the obtained system for variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** To find the initial variables\n\n$$\nx_1(t) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad x_2(t)\n$$\n\nsatisfying the original initial value problem, apply the inverse Laplace transform to \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\nLet's see how this works in practice." :tutorial/id #uuid "98573e3a-ebcd-565e-8de7-a83e3deb9d09" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14610 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "f663bde1-a39c-5d4d-83fd-15b833a5cbea" :step/math-academy-id 590687 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167886}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167006}]}
